  "description": "Instructional affine screen projection of the source's already worked exercise53: complete tetrahedron ABCD and section NMQP. This is not an extra solution added to an unsolved question. All eight named vertices/section points, six whole tetrahedron edges and four section sides are retained. BC and NP remain dashed. Incidence and parallel assertions describe the displayed affine projection, not a reconstructed metric spatial model. AD's crossings with hatch strokes or NP are screen crossings only, not additional physical cutting-plane intersections. Coordinates, light fill and seven evenly spaced inset hatch strokes are modern layout regularization, not source-given lengths, ratios or a certified printed hatch count. No ticks, measurements, new labels or answer text are drawn.",
